                  "name": "Story Paragraph",
                  "fill": "#8FA2B8",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The Mars Exploration Rover mission dispatched twin mobile robot geologists to opposite sides of Mars under NASA's 'Follow the Water' charter. Before MER, evidence for liquid surface water was speculative, derived from orbital valley channels. Spirit and Opportunity directly sampled the sedimentary and geochemical record, confirming that Mars once hosted persistent, active aquatic environments.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 11.5,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
